                <pb facs="0631" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 723.2515/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-11T01:00:00+00:00"
                            >January 11, 1919—1 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>237. [From Lansing.] Your 23 December 13, 5 p.m. The President doubts the wisdom
                    of a Bolivian deputation either to the United States or to Paris at the present
                    juncture. Lansing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
